    "cargo_lock": {
      "comment": [
        "Narrowed from a whole-file hash to the dependency closure of the",
        "packages that actually produce a shipped artifact. native/ is now a",
        "six-member workspace sharing one lock file, so a dependency added to",
        "a member that ships nothing - uuav-abi-smoke's libloading, say - moved",
        "the whole-file hash and demanded a macOS *and* a Windows rebuild of a",
        "byte-identical core. The closure digest moves exactly when the set of",
        "crates compiled into a shipped binary moves, which is the property the",
        "lock was always trying to express.",
        "Verified when this was narrowed: the closure of ['uuav'] is identical",
        "in the working tree and at the commit the shipped binaries were built",
        "from (4baa042a..., 80 packages), while the whole-file hash had already",
        "moved. So this is a re-expression of the same fact, not a relock.",
        "At M6, when uuav-client becomes the shipped library and uuav-adapter",
        "the shipped child, roots becomes [uuav, uuav-client, uuav-adapter]."
      ],
      "kind": "cargo-lock-closure",
